Guard the strerror_r run test for cross builds

The XSI-vs-GNU strerror_r probe compiles and runs a test application;
nativesdk builds have no exe_wrapper, so meson fails at configure time
with "Can not run test applications in this cross environment". Fall
back to the XSI variant when cross compiling (what glibc provides
without _GNU_SOURCE, and what the qemu-mediated target probe selects
for the same glibc sysroot).

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -310,11 +310,17 @@
     return strerror_r (EINVAL, buf, 32);
 }
 '''
-  strerror_r_check = cc.run(strerror_r_code, name : 'strerror_r check')
-  if strerror_r_check.returncode() == 0
-    conf.set('HAVE_XSI_STRERROR_R', 1)
+  if not meson.is_cross_build()
+    strerror_r_check = cc.run(strerror_r_code, name : 'strerror_r check')
+    if strerror_r_check.returncode() == 0
+      conf.set('HAVE_XSI_STRERROR_R', 1)
+    else
+      conf.set('HAVE_GNU_STRERROR_R', 1)
+    endif
   else
-    conf.set('HAVE_GNU_STRERROR_R', 1)
+    # cannot run test applications when cross compiling; assume the
+    # XSI variant, which is what glibc provides without _GNU_SOURCE
+    conf.set('HAVE_XSI_STRERROR_R', 1)
   endif
 endif
 
